<h1 id="wo-03-complete-queries-bounded-pages-and-authorized-statistics">WO-03 — Complete queries, bounded pages and authorized statistics</h1>
<h2 id="summary">Summary</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Planning only.</strong> R04, R06, R07 and R08 remain <strong>OPEN</strong> at source baseline <code>9fae3248aadecaa53198a5fb9f06576fdcc182cf</code>. No implementation, test run, migration or deployment was performed while preparing this work order.</li><li>18 atomic tasks, each with an owner, prerequisites and a write set of at most five files. Critical path: query contract → data/index preflight → repository boundaries → page/deep-link flows → independent acceptance.</li><li>Preserve Riverpod and <code>presentation -&gt; domain &lt;- data</code>. Aggregate access must never grant access to personal user documents.</li><li>Proposed measurable acceptance budgets: 50 records/page, at most 100 mounted episode rows, at most 200 documents per search/export batch. These are design limits for synthetic verification, <strong>not measured performance improvements</strong>.</li><li>Blast radius: high, spanning four reading flows, a Flutter domain interface, one aggregate callable, indexes and a conditional data repair tool. No new dependency, lockfile change, file deletion or deployment is planned.</li></ul>
<h2 id="document-information">Document information</h2>
<p>Date: 2026-10-25. Owner: Boss Scrum/Tech Lead. Inputs: [technical review](tech-review.md), [master plan](execution-plan.md), and existing project contracts. There is no review-specific PRD; do not invent one. Paths below are relative to <code>hudhud_fm</code>. <strong>NEW</strong> means a proposed file that does not yet exist. The user's English language instruction overrides the default Boss artifact language.</p>
<h2 id="0-repository-preflight">0. Repository preflight</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Fact</th><th>Evidence / result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Current/default branches</td><td><code>hudhud_fm</code> / <code>refs/remotes/origin/main</code>, read using <code>git branch --show-current</code> and <code>git symbolic-ref refs/remotes/origin/HEAD</code></td></tr><tr><td>Source validation</td><td>R04/R06/R07/R08 implementation paths were reread and remain present. Production dataset size was not inspected</td></tr><tr><td>CI</td><td><code>.github/workflows</code> absent in this inspection. Use actual package scripts and quality contract; do not invent a CI pass</td></tr><tr><td>Flutter R04</td><td><code>StationContentFirestoreDataSource.readEpisodes</code> applies limit100 before publication filtering/order; <code>FirebaseStationContentRepository._read</code> filters and sorts afterwards; repository interface exposes only <code>readCache/refresh</code></td></tr><tr><td>Flutter deep link</td><td><code>lib/features/notifications/presentation/episode_alert_navigation.dart</code> searches the first refresh batch; <code>lib/features/station_details/presentation/station_details_screen.dart</code> passes an episode list to <code>ProgramDetailsScreen</code></td></tr><tr><td>Admin R06</td><td><code>admin-app.tsx:1088–1089</code> uses server cursors only for reports and caps others at2000; search, export and totals derive from loaded records</td></tr><tr><td>Count R07</td><td><code>UsersAggregateView</code> is routed for non-super-admins but counts the users collection directly; <code>firestore.rules:284–286</code> grants users list only to super admins</td></tr><tr><td>Public R08</td><td><code>content-repository.ts:9</code> has no limit; mapping and <code>station-detail.tsx:44–46</code> repeatedly scan archives per program</td></tr><tr><td>Schema/authority</td><td><code>functions/lib/admin-content.js</code>, <code>web_hudhud/lib/discovery.ts</code>, <code>EpisodeMapper/ProgramMapper</code>, Rules and <code>docs/contracts/firebase-data-contract.md</code>. Verified server token claims determine role, never request payload</td></tr><tr><td>Verification entry points</td><td>Flutter targeted suites; package scripts in both web apps/functions; root <code>npm run emulators:admin</code></td></tr><tr><td>Migration risk</td><td>Firestore orderBy excludes documents missing its field. No production audit performed; check publication/time/priority fields before enabling new ordering</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2 id="1-scope-and-agreed-behavior-to-establish">1. Scope and agreed behavior to establish</h2>
<h3 id="1-1-page-search-count-and-export-contract">1.1 Page, search, count and export contract</h3>
<ol><li><strong>Episodes:</strong> filter server-side by stationId and <code>isPublished == true</code>, plus programId on a program page. Stable order: <code>broadcastAt DESC, priority DESC, documentId ASC</code>. T01 must explicitly document public-web tie-order changing from title to this tuple; Flutter priority tie semantics remain. Missing ordering fields are addressed in section1.3 before activation.</li><li><strong>Programs:</strong> bounded independent active-program pages. Preserve featured/priority ordering only after checking all required fields and indexes, with document ID as tie-breaker. T01 must settle this before implementation; do not claim global ordering by sorting a partial page locally.</li><li><strong>Page size:</strong>50 episodes or programs/request. One page request/user action; no automatic unbounded loop skipping drafts/invalid mappings. Cursor advances from the last raw document even when mapping rejects it. An empty mapped page with a cursor is not end-of-data. One lookahead document is permitted, making the return budget51.</li><li><strong>State:</strong> initialLoading/ready/loadingMore/offline/error. A later-page error preserves existing content. Deduplicate IDs. Station/program/filter changes or refresh invalidate cursors and stale completions. Domain must not expose Firebase snapshots: use an opaque value cursor with version, root, station/program, filter fingerprint and sort tuple; reject cross-scope reuse.</li><li><strong>Deep links:</strong> fetch the target episode directly, then validate its parent program/station, root, publication/deletion state and canonical IDs. Do not scan pages until episode10000. No autoplay. Foreign/draft targets show unavailable. A partial station page is not proof a program has no episodes.</li><li><strong>Admin pages:</strong> server pages50 for non-report resources too; preserve collection-group root bounds before limit. Global sort must be expressed in supported queries. An old sorting option requiring absent fields/indexes must receive an explicit contract decision, not a misleading local sort.</li><li><strong>Admin text search:</strong> Firestore has no arbitrary full-text contains query. Preserve the existing match predicate through two explicit modes: clearly labeled current-page search, and user-started resumable full-dataset scanning. Full scanning reads at most200 documents/continuation, displays “N examined, M matched so far,” supports continue/cancel, and never calls M a complete total before exhaustion. It can reach record2001/10000 without loading all records at once. Freeze filter/sort fingerprint and invalidate changed searches. T01 is the decision gate for this UX; if not accepted, record the alternative and new write set before dispatch. Do not silently substitute page search for global search acceptance.</li><li><strong>Counts:</strong> server-filter total excludes unindexed free-text search; show asOf and distinguish matched-so-far. R07 proposes callable <code>adminGetUserCount</code>, returning only <code>{root,total,asOf}</code>. It accepts verified, authorized super_admin/station_admin/moderator identities using the existing authority convention and root allowlist. A listener, document owner or other user cannot obtain administrative statistics. The allowed root-level total exposes no IDs, email, documents or personal breakdowns.</li><li><strong>Exports:</strong> “Export current page” exports exactly that page. “Export all matching results” performs an independent bounded cursor scan with frozen filters, start time, cancel/resume and progress. Write parts of at most1000 records each; fetch at most200/request; do not retain a10000-row array. Manifest identifies scope, counts and completeness. This is not a transactionally fixed snapshot under concurrent writes; disclose that and test complete equality on a fixed fixture. Use WO-01-authorized projections, never confidential fields unavailable to the actor.</li></ol>
<h3 id="1-2-synthetic-acceptance-budgets">1.2 Synthetic acceptance budgets</h3>
<table><thead><tr><th>Journey</th><th>Proposed measurable budget</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Initial public station content</td><td>One programs query≤51 documents + one episodes query≤51; never read10000</td></tr><tr><td>Open program / next page</td><td>One episode query≤51, plus a direct parent read if not already loaded</td></tr><tr><td>Distant episode link</td><td>At most3 document reads: station/program/episode; no page traversal</td></tr><tr><td>Admin ordinary page</td><td>At most51 resource documents; relation hydration restricted to page IDs, <code>in</code> chunks≤30; count does not download profiles</td></tr><tr><td>Full text search</td><td>At most200 documents per explicit continuation; visible result window≤100; no full-archive accumulation</td></tr><tr><td>Full export</td><td>At most200 documents/request; at most1000 live records before writing a part; count/scope manifest</td></tr><tr><td>Public render</td><td>At most100 mounted episode rows using previous/next or a bounded window; group by program once per page change, not every clock tick</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>Returned-document counts are not billed index-read counts. Instrument calls/documents/rows; any latency/memory measurement must name its device/environment and is supplementary, with no invented speedup percentage. Fixtures:101+ mixed draft/published documents for R04;2001+ matching records for each R06 resource;10000 episodes over multiple programs for R08. Include empty programs, drafts, deleted entries, equal timestamps, missing legacy fields and concurrent insert/delete/reorder between pages. Under mutation: deduplicate, invalidate/restart when query identity changes, and expose refresh for records moved before the cursor; do not promise snapshot isolation that Firestore pages lack.</p>
<h3 id="1-3-index-migration-and-rollback-preflight">1.3 Index, migration and rollback preflight</h3>
<ul><li>Audit each root separately with bounded cursor reads: presence/type of broadcastAt, priority, isPublished, isActive, isFeatured and parent references. Report counts without personal payloads. Any authorized apply operation stores its access-restricted backup separately, not in review logs.</li><li>Never fabricate broadcastAt from now or an unrelated timestamp to include a legacy record in ordering. Unresolvable entries require an explicit data-owner decision and remain visible to an administrative repair process. Default priority0 is allowed only after agreement with mappers/validators. Document contract disagreement before implementation.</li><li>Tools default to dry-run with explicit root and scan budget; tests use demo projects only. Future authorized apply requires a separate apply switch, backup and resume token. Use version/preimage-conditional transactions; never overwrite newer edits. No broad delete.</li><li>Add indexes only after enumerating actual query shapes, including station/program/publication/sort tuple and necessary root-bounded collection groups. Owner integrates additive changes in <code>firestore.indexes.json</code>. Emulator success does not establish deployed composite-index readiness; future authorized rollout must wait for readiness.</li><li>Rollout sequence if separately authorized: legacy audit → approved repair if needed → additive index readiness → compatible aggregate server → new clients. Keep old read compatibility until acceptance; do not reuse legacy cursors in new queries.</li><li>Rollback: restore a known client version while disclosing its old limits, retain additive indexes initially, disable new page behavior without opening permissions. Restore data only when the current post-image/version still matches the migration's write; otherwise report conflict. Never restore WO-01 private fields into public documents. No rollout/rollback command is run during planning.</li></ul>
<h2 id="2-atomic-tasks-and-owned-write-sets">2. Atomic tasks and owned write sets</h2>
<p>Every task is <strong>PLANNED</strong>. E=edit existing; N=<strong>NEW</strong> proposed. The named owner owns every file in its row. Overlapping rows are explicitly sequential; writes outside the declared set require a revised plan.</p>
